usage: tracker_query.py [-h] [-b] [-t URL] [-H HEX] [-e EVENT] [-o FORMAT] [-f FILE] [-p] [-r] [-n NUM] [-d SECONDS]

Query a BitTorrent tracker announce endpoint and display swarm info (seeds, leechers, peers). Supports HTTP/HTTPS and UDP trackers.

optional arguments:
  -h, --help                   show this help message and exit
  -b, --batch                  Enable batch mode to query multiple trackers from a file (ignores --tracker and --format) (default: False)
  -t URL, --tracker URL        Tracker announce URL (http://, https://, or udp://). Ignored in batch mode. (default: udp://open.stealth.si:80/announce)
  -H HEX, --hash HEX           Info hash (40 hex characters) (default: 5CB6C44712D494A87E8554839FB0541046B157AF)
  -e EVENT, --event EVENT      Announce event type (default: started)
  -o FORMAT, --format FORMAT   Output format: table, json, or csv. (default: table)
  -f FILE, --file FILE         Tracker list file for batch mode (one tracker URL per line, # for comments) (default: trackers_to_query.txt)
  -p, --show-peers             Display the full list of peers (IP:port) (default: False)
  -r, --random-qb              Use a random qBittorrent client version for the announce (spoofs User-Agent and peer_id) (default: False)
  -n NUM, --num-want NUM       Number of peers to request from tracker (default: 50)
  -d SECONDS, --delay SECONDS  Delay between queries in batch mode (in seconds). Ignored in single-tracker mode. (default: 1.0)
